Suppose additionally that for $m = EE[X]$ there are $a, b in RR$ with $f(x) > a x + b$ for all $x in RR \\ {m}$ and $f(m) = a m + b$. Since $f(X) - (a X + b) >= 0$, equality $EE[f(X)] = f(EE[X])$ forces
$
  EE[f(X)- (a X + b)] = 0,
$
and a non-negative random variable with zero expectation vanishes almost surely: $PP(f(X) - (a X + b) = 0) = 1$. By the strictness property of the supporting line this is equivalent to
$
  PP(X = m) = 1.
$
